---
import LegalDocument from '../../components/LegalDocument.astro';
import { legalDates, legalUrls } from '../../lib/legal';
const { canonical, alternate } = legalUrls('en', '/privacy', '/privacy');
---
<LegalDocument lang="en" title="Privacy Policy" metaTitle="Privacy Policy | Repero AI" description="How Repero AI processes personal data on its public website and in its service." canonical={canonical} alternate={alternate} lastUpdated={legalDates.en} eyebrow="Privacy">
  <p>This policy describes the categories of personal data Repero processes when you visit <strong>repero.ai</strong>, contact us, or use Repero AI. It distinguishes the public website from product-side operations at <strong>app.repero.ai</strong>.</p>
  <aside class="legal-document__notice" aria-label="Publication status"><p><strong>Publication status.</strong> The legal identity, registered address, enterprise/VAT details and designated privacy contact for the controller have not yet been confirmed for publication. They must be completed before commercial publication. This policy does not claim GDPR compliance merely by being published.</p></aside>
  <h2>1. Controller and contact</h2>
  <p>The controller for the relevant processing must be identified in the legal notice before commercial publication. The owner must also publish a contact method for privacy requests. Until those facts are confirmed, do not rely on this page as a complete controller-identification notice.</p>
  <h2>2. Processing at a glance</h2>
  <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Activity</th><th scope="col">Data categories</th><th scope="col">Purpose and legal basis</th><th scope="col">Recipients and retention</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Website delivery and security</td><td>IP address, browser/device information, request data, security events</td><td>Deliver and protect the website; legitimate interests and, where applicable, legal obligations</td><td>Cloudflare edge services are used for the public website. Data is kept only as needed for delivery, security, incident handling, and applicable obligations.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Account and authentication</td><td>Account identifiers, email address, display/profile data, authentication and session-security data</td><td>Create and secure access to the service; performance of a contract and legitimate interests in security</td><td>Product providers are not confirmed in this repository. Retention must follow the applicable account and deletion policy.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Workspace and user content</td><td>Workspace/project metadata, prompts, conversations, documents, sources, generated artefacts, and related metadata</td><td>Provide requested storage, organization, retrieval, and AI-assisted functionality; performance of a contract</td><td>Infrastructure and AI-provider arrangements require confirmation. Content is retained only for the relevant service purpose, subject to deletion, backup, security, and legal requirements.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Technical, security, and usage data</td><td>Logs, timestamps, request metadata, error/performance data, and security events</td><td>Operate, secure, troubleshoot, and improve reliability; legitimate interests and legal obligations where applicable</td><td>Recipients and exact schedules require confirmation. Retention is limited to what is necessary for those purposes.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Billing</td><td>Billing contact, plan, invoices, tax and payment-status data</td><td>Administer a paid service and meet accounting obligations; contract and legal obligation</td><td>Only applicable if paid plans are enabled. Payment provider and retention details are pending commercial decisions.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Support and contact requests</td><td>Contact details and the information included in a request</td><td>Respond to and document requests; contract, legitimate interests, or consent as applicable</td><td>Recipients and retention are limited to the support purpose and applicable obligations.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h2>3. AI-assisted functionality</h2>
  <p>Repero uses AI systems and generative models to provide requested functionality. Depending on the feature, user-provided prompts, documents, retrieved passages, metadata, and other relevant context may be processed as necessary to perform that request.</p>
  <p>Repero may use different models or providers depending on product configuration. This public repository does not confirm the providers enabled in production, their data locations, or their processing terms. Repero does not make a claim here about provider training, model retention, encryption, or geographic processing.</p>
  <p>AI outputs can be incomplete, incorrect, or misleading. Users should review outputs when accuracy, safety, legal, financial, medical, professional, or other material decisions are involved. See <a href="/en/trust/ai">AI transparency</a>.</p>
  <h2>4. Optional communications</h2>
  <p>Marketing or newsletter communications are not currently evidenced as active on this public site. If introduced, they will be described separately and sent only on the appropriate legal basis, including consent where required. Withdrawal will be made available as easily as possible.</p>
  <h2>5. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>The audited site code does not intentionally deploy analytics, marketing cookies, local storage, or session storage. Cloudflare edge/security technologies may apply where necessary. See the <a href="/en/cookies">Cookies Policy</a> for the current public-site position.</p>
  <h2>6. Recipients, subprocessors, and transfers</h2>
  <p>Personal data may be made available to service providers necessary to run the website or service, under appropriate arrangements where required. Confirmed public-site infrastructure is Cloudflare Pages/edge delivery; optional waitlist storage uses Cloudflare D1 only if that unused endpoint is activated.</p>
  <p>The production inventory for authentication, model providers, storage, databases, observability, email, payment, and other subprocessors has not yet been confirmed from <strong>ai-platform</strong>. A public provider list will not be published until that audit is complete. International-transfer details will be added only after they are confirmed.</p>
  <h2>7. Retention</h2>
  <p>Repero should retain personal data only for the period necessary for the relevant purpose, including service delivery, security, dispute handling, and legal or accounting obligations. Exact schedules, backup handling, deletion jobs, and post-termination export behavior remain operational decisions to be confirmed in the product.</p>
  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Subject to applicable law, individuals may have rights to access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection, portability, and withdrawal of consent where processing relies on consent. They may also lodge a complaint with the competent data-protection authority.</p>
  <p>A verified contact channel and a product-side rights-request process are still required. Those operations belong to <strong>app.repero.ai</strong> and are not implemented by this static website.</p>
  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>Repero may update this policy when processing, providers, or legal requirements change. The last-updated date will be revised and material changes should be communicated through an appropriate channel.</p>
</LegalDocument>
